mbedTLS 4.1.1 TLS 1.3 client: accept a cookie in a HelloRetryRequest and echo it (RFC 8446 4.2.2).
mbedtls_ssl_tls13_check_received_extension() lets a server's extension through only if the client
sent it, and a client never sends a cookie in its first ClientHello, so every HelloRetryRequest with
a cookie ends in unsupported_extension (Mbed-TLS/mbedtls#9543). The client already stores the cookie
(ssl_tls13_parse_cookie_ext()) and echoes it in the second ClientHello (ssl_tls13_write_cookie_ext()).
Applies to espressif/mbedtls 3deef6a6 (esp-pqc 95db07d1) and to stock mbedTLS 4.1.1 (ce3f3485).
Applied at configure time by ../mbedtls_patches.cmake.

--- a/library/ssl_tls13_generic.c
+++ b/library/ssl_tls13_generic.c
@@ -1697,6 +1697,16 @@
     }
 
     ssl->handshake->received_extensions |= extension_mask;
+    /*
+     * RFC 8446 section 4.2.2: a server MAY send a cookie in a HelloRetryRequest
+     * although the client sent none; the client echoes it in its second
+     * ClientHello (ssl_tls13_write_cookie_ext()).
+     */
+    if (hs_msg_type == MBEDTLS_SSL_TLS1_3_HS_HELLO_RETRY_REQUEST &&
+        received_extension_type == MBEDTLS_TLS_EXT_COOKIE) {
+        return 0;
+    }
+
     /*
      * If it is a message containing extension responses, check that we
      * previously sent the extension.
